      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Here's some more thoughts on this idea:\nAdd an aditional bool for 'Low priority' messages, defaults to false so that older OSC apps still perform as expected, backwards compatible.\nHave a quick menu item in the Chatbox section to 'Hide low priority messages', or ideally, copy the existing size/opacity/duration settings for low priority messages.\nIn my eyes... This is extremely easy to implement and has no negative effect on existing OSC apps, nor does it affect any apps already in development. On the VRC side, it's literally just copy-pasting a menu item and adding a config entry that it's changing right?\nIf something to prevent chatbox's filling the sky can't be implemented and you want this feature removed from OVR Toolkit until that time, please don't hesitate to let me know!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
