      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This **needs** to be a thing. As a chatbox user, I'm really sick of hearing people say they turned chatboxes off because they don't want to see people's music statuses. People who use the chatbox for \"now playing\" messages directly affect my ability to communicate with people.\n\nThese types of messages need to be treated differently from actual communication messages. Whether that be giving them \"low priority\" tags or creating another system on nameplates that serves the same purpose.\n\n(By the way, if you're reading this and you use these status messages, I kindly and politely ask you to stop and spread the word until low priority messages are a thing. I, all other mutes, and people who don't want unecessary text on-screen would genuinely really appreciate it. Thanks!)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
